@layer 2
@aid_version 0.2
@purpose Type checker for Aria — enforces static typing with effect polymorphism, Result-typed error flow, trait bounds, and generic monomorphization via a multi-pass AST traversal. Canonicalises container types through a deduplicating TypeStore to prevent memory explosion during bootstrap self-compilation.
@depends [parser, resolver, diagnostic]

---

@workflow type_check_pipeline
@purpose token stream + DeclIndex -> typed store + registries + diagnostics
@steps
  1. Pre-pass: scan tokens for `effect Name implies Parent` directives, register as trait defs. [src: checker.aria:5181-5207]
  2. Pass 1 (type registration): pre-register struct/enum names for forward references, then walk DeclIndex and register fields with resolved type IDs. [src: checker.aria:597-653]
  3. Pass 2 (function signatures): iterate DeclIndex, parse fn annotations (@deprecated, @cold), extract params/return/error types + effect annotations into FnSig. [src: checker.aria:1191-1271]
  4. Pass 3 (body checking): traverse fn bodies checking statements/expressions against context (return type, error type, in_loop, in_callee_slot). Emits diagnostics. [src: checker.aria:2539]
  5. Pass 4 (once-closure consumption): linear scan enforcing linear-type invariants for `once` values. [src: checker.aria:5162-5225]

@workflow trait_resolution
@purpose How operator dispatch is resolved to an impl
@steps
  1. Call site hits type_supports_op(treg, store, type_id, op). [src: traits.aria:337-359]
  2. Logical (`&&`, `||`) and bitwise ops short-circuit via is_integer() / is_bool(). [src: traits.aria:339-345]
  3. Trait-based ops map op -> trait via op_requires_trait() (e.g. `+` -> Add). [src: traits.aria:325-334]
  4. treg_has_impl(treg, type_name, trait_name): hash-index fast path, linear-scan fallback. [src: traits.aria:130-144]
  5. Return bool; error only emitted at call site if the op was required.

@workflow generic_monomorphization
@purpose Polymorphic call -> specialized type assignment
@steps
  1. On call to a generic fn, read generic_count and generic_name_0..2 from FnSig. [src: checker.aria:4217]
  2. Check each type arg satisfies its bound via treg_has_impl. [src: checker.aria:4043-4083]
  3. Create MonoSpec(generic_name, specialized_name, type_arg_0..2) and register with the mono registry. [src: checker.aria:4217-4480]
  4. substitute_type() rewrites param/return types using the type-var map. [src: types.aria:336-360]

---

@invariants
  TypeStore deduplication guardrail: container types (Array, Optional, Result, Tuple, Applied) are canonicalized; if store.types.len() >= STORE_CAP (500000) the add bails to TY_UNKNOWN rather than OOM. [src: types.aria:245-262]
  Env parallel-arrays invariant: env_names, env_types, env_scopes all have equal length. Lookup walks backwards to find the most recent binding. [src: checker.aria:29-32]
  Pre-registration ordering: user-defined types must be pre-registered in pass 1 before resolve_type_name is called against them. Calling too early returns TY_UNKNOWN. [src: checker.aria:597-653]
  Scope cleanup: _env_trim(saved_len) reconstructs env arrays from indices 1..saved_len, dropping inner bindings on block exit. [src: checker.aria:231-248]
  Trait hash index is best-effort: treg_find_impl falls back to a linear scan starting at index 1 when the hash index is stale during pass-1/2 registration. [src: traits.aria:113-144]
  Generic-name HKT suffix `[_]` distinguishes higher-kinded parameters; _mk_typevar_from_name and _strip_hkt_suffix must be used consistently. [src: checker.aria:713-730]

---

@antipatterns
  Calling store_add() on a container type bypasses canonicalization and can explode the store. Always use store_add_canonical(). [src: types.aria:245-262]
  Using == on type IDs to compare types: container IDs can differ while representing the same type. Use types_equal(). [src: types.aria:314-332]
  Calling resolve_type_name on a user type before pass 1 completes returns TY_UNKNOWN — downstream diagnostics become misleading "type not found" errors. [src: checker.aria:597-653]
  Calling populate_builtins on a non-empty TraitRegistry: no dedup, duplicate impls accumulate and trait-resolution lookups become nondeterministic. [src: traits.aria:238-321]
  Mixing _resolve_type_node (AST-based) and _parse_type_ann (token-based) in the same pass: they diverge on HKT generics and edge-case types. [src: checker.aria:252, checker.aria:703]

